Network Devices and Their Functions

Hubs: These devices broadcast information to every connected device on a network, similar to a radio tower.
Switches: More intelligent than hubs, switches create specific connections between devices, sending data only to the intended recipient, which enhances security and network performance.
Connecting Networks and the Internet

Routers: Routers connect multiple networks, directing information between them by reading destination addresses and forwarding data to the appropriate network's router.
Modems: These devices connect your router to the internet, enabling internet access for your local area network (LAN) and facilitating communication with devices in different geographic locations.
Virtualization in Networking

Virtualization Tools: Beyond physical devices, software-based virtualization tools can perform the functions of hubs, switches, routers, and modems. These tools, often offered by cloud service providers, provide cost savings and scalability in network operations.
